                <pb facs="0412" n="300" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg300"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/5229: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Commission to
                        Negotiate Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-27"><hi rendition="#italic">September 27,
                        1919</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>3259. For Polk.</p>
                <p>Department’s 3198, September 22. We have been advised that Treasury has funds
                    available provided plan for withdrawal of Czecho-Slovak troops is approved.
                    Early decision urgent or it will be too late to move the men before winter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
